{"agent":"ph-parity","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The `verified.unverified` array is supposed to hold only unverified facts, but this entry records a *documented absence*: “session-start and session-end hooks (documented absent)”. A consumer or conformance check that reads `verified.unverified` as the set of unknowns will therefore treat the session-hook gap as unknown rather than as a known absence. That violates the three-valued facts requirement (value, documented absent, unverified): given a check that asks whether session hooks are unverified, the descriptor answers “yes” because of line 129, even though the same file and the research intent say they are documented absent.","digest":"32eb58fbcc272350","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/harnesses/vibe.toml:129","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/harnesses/vibe.toml:129"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The test asserts the complete documented hook event set is exactly `{\"pre_tool\": \"pre_tool\", \"post_tool\": \"post_tool\"}`, but the change intent and manifest state that Vibe hooks are documented with `pre_tool`, `post_tool`, and `post_agent`. If the descriptor records the documented `post_agent` event, this exact-equality assertion fails; if it omits `post_agent`, the test certifies an incomplete descriptor and hides a documented fact.","digest":"223ad6b62de83086","family":"alibaba","location":"tests/test_harness_vibe.py:16","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_harness_vibe.py:16"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":12955,"diff_sha":"44f2e1988e89ec705ed05c72e7273d7dc1cc1197e32b002a790dfd6105a953eb","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/VB-descriptor","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":0.8,"family":"alibaba","finding